From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Renato <remourato@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:44:04 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(context): read Chromium-family browsers and Safari, and
 let Quick Actions use the page

Browser context now targets a checked table of browsers (Helium, Chrome channels, Chromium,
Arc, Safari, Safari Technology Preview) instead of Helium alone. Safari tabs bind window id,
tab index and URL and re-verify the URL before reading. A switched-off "Allow JavaScript from
Apple Events" maps to its own failure with the browser's menu path, and every failure names the
browser. Quick Actions fall back to the active tab's selection or text when no selection is
found and browser context is on, always opening the result panel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
